 - `rerenderMessage(timestamp)`: draws the assistant reply with that `message.timestamp` again, re-running the [assistant text renderers](#assistant-text-renderer); a no-op while `extensionRenderers.assistantText` is off
 - `getLinkClicksAvailable()`: whether picking a [claimed link](#extension-link-schemes), by its hint tag or a click, raises `link_activate` right now
 
+`ctx.ui.registerRemoteUi` is available in the interactive TUI. It registers one
+extension-owned transport for selector, editor, approval and ask dialogs. The
+returned disposer unregisters the transport; call it on `session_shutdown` and
+when reloading the extension. A second registration throws.
+
+The handler receives a select or editor request and an abort signal. Return
+`{ kind: "answered", value }` only for an explicit remote action. An undefined
+value means explicit cancellation. Return `{ kind: "unavailable" }` when the
+transport cannot answer. An error or invalid selection is also unavailable, so
+the local dialog remains open.
+
+The first answer from the local dialog, the registered transport or Collab wins.
+Stop remote work when the signal aborts. The transport must authenticate its
+clients and protect requests and answers: an approval can allow a tool to run.
+Secret input dialogs are not mirrored by this API.
+
 Current no-op methods in this controller:
 
 - `setFooter`
